{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"illusory-patronal-giraffe","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Advisory from S6 (6f14) LLM code review (Gerrit 1850). When the op-cert signer is composed from the inline-PEM source REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY (src/rebar/opcert_service/config.py from_env), the raw Ed25519 private key remains in os.environ for the process lifetime and is inherited by every child process (ssh-keygen subprocesses in keyprov, git pushes). The DEPLOYED path uses REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH (a mounted 0600 file), not inline PEM, so this affects only the secondary/dev inline-PEM path. Remediation: after compose_signer consumes private_key, pop REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY from os.environ without breaking config-reload semantics. Deferred from S6 to avoid rushing a config-load side-effect change on a non-deployed path.","id":"932d-52d8-1d59-426c","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Harden op-cert inline-PEM path: unset REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY from os.environ after compose"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787036454809590001,"uuid":"f39e4c21-2ab4-4a5c-ac28-5f42e6bf8af9"}